8ee1e19085" 13194139533488 17592186045585 true] [17592186402209 1081 "4" 13194139533488 17592186045585 true] [17592186402209 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533488 17592186045585 true] [17592186402209 1084 #uuid "b2b777f7-364c-5626-889b-acd8d2432b4f" 13194139533488 17592186045585 true] [17592186402210 1081 "0" 13194139533488 17592186045585 true] [17592186402210 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533488 17592186045585 true] [17592186402210 1084 #uuid "f86c81e4-5ffc-590a-bee6-c31a2b4d7942" 13194139533488 17592186045585 true] [17592186402211 1081 "-1" 13194139533488 17592186045585 true] [17592186402211 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533488 17592186045585 true] [17592186402211 1084 #uuid "26b4b7f1-4d1e-5d04-a085-a90adb893d85" 13194139533488 17592186045585 true] [17592186402212 1081 "-2" 13194139533488 17592186045585 true] [17592186402212 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533488 17592186045585 true] [17592186402212 1084 #uuid "88cb0c2c-4eb3-51aa-922a-e0d82d33d145" 13194139533488 17592186045585 true] [17592186402213 1068 #edb/ref 17592186402214 13194139533488 17592186045585 true] [17592186402213 1069 "q-338587" 13194139533488 17592186045585 true] [17592186402213 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533488 17592186045585 true] [17592186402213 1071 "Which of the following systems is a boundary value problem?\n\nI. $4{y}^{″}-{y}^{′}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x),\\,y(0)=1$\nII. ${y}^{″}+xy={e}^{x},\\,y(1)=0,\\,y(3)=2$\nIII. ${y}^{″}={x}^{3},\\,y(2)=5$" 13194139533488 17592186045585 true] [17592186402213 1072 #uuid "a42fad0a-c170-522e-8f97-0f501aa9bc73" 13194139533488 17592186045585 true] [17592186402213 1074 "If a second-order differential equation for the function $y(x)$ is given with two conditions specified at *different* locations in the domain of $y,$ then this is a **boundary value problem**.\n\nLet's go through each equation in turn.\n\n- The first system is not a boundary value problem. It consists of a differential equation combined with only one condition.\n\n- The second system is a boundary value problem. It consists of a differential equation together with two conditions at different points in the domain of $y(x)$ (i.e., at $x=1$ and $x=3$).\n\n- The third system is not a boundary value problem. It consists of a differential equation combined with only one condition." 13194139533488 17592186045585 true] [17592186402214 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402215 13194139533488 17592186045585 true] [17592186402214 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402216 13194139533488 17592186045585 true] [17592186402214 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402217 13194139533488 17592186045585 true] [17592186402214 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402218 13194139533488 17592186045585 true] [17592186402214 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402219 13194139533488 17592186045585 true] [17592186402214 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533488 17592186045585 true] [17592186402214 1077 "selection" 13194139533488 17592186045585 true] [17592186402214 1079 #edb/ref 17592186402219 13194139533488 17592186045585 true] [17592186402214 1080 #uuid "acf1e061-7a98-5801-95c8-22217b716f6a" 13194139533488 17592186045585 true] [17592186402215 1081 "II and III only" 13194139533488 17592186045585 true] [17592186402215 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533488 17592186045585 true] [17592186402215 1084 #uuid "7fd99f64-1a0e-5d84-8e13-95caae8d936d" 13194139533488 17592186045585 true] [17592186402216 1081 "I and III only" 13194139533488 17592186045585 true] [17592186402216 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533488 17592186045585 true] [17592186402216 1084 #uuid "8b10290b-80cb-5b29-9f79-1f195229c212" 13194139533488 17592186045585 true] [17592186402217 1081 "I only" 13194139533488 17592186045585 true] [17592186402217 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533488 17592186045585 true] [17592186402217 1084 #uuid "05e09efb-9144-55ca-b467-bbf73a07f532" 13194139533488 17592186045585 true] [17592186402218 1081 "I and II only" 13194139533488 17592186045585 true] [17592186402218 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533488 17592186045585 true] [17592186402218 1084 #uuid "49d1e9f7-e09c-5fb0-9b7e-39e20b2c166e" 13194139533488 17592186045585 true] [17592186402219 1081 "II only" 13194139533488 17592186045585 true] [17592186402219 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533488 17592186045585 true] [17592186402219 1084 #uuid "9983cf80-2f24-55d7-be17-9eb6b4c84e81" 13194139533488 17592186045585 true] [17592186402220 1068 #edb/ref 17592186402221 13194139533488 17592186045585 true] [17592186402220 1069 "q-338623" 13194139533488 17592186045585 true] [17592186402220 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533488 17592186045585 true] [17592186402220 1071 "Consider the following boundary value problem.\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}(x)-{y}^{′}(x)+y(x)={x}^{2},\\,y(1)=0,\\,3y(3)+{y}^{′}(3)=6,\\,1\\le x\\le 3\n$$\n\nWhich of the following best classifies the boundary conditions for this problem?" 13194139533488 17592186045585 true] [17592186402220 1072 #uuid "dc494029-58f4-51d4-95fe-9c9b2384d2b2" 13194139533488 17592186045585 true] [17592186402220 1074 "For a second-order boundary value problem, \n\n$$\n{y}^{″}(x)+P(x){y}^{′}(x)+Q(x)y(x)=f(x),\\,a\\le x\\le b\n$$\n\nwhere $P(x),Q(x)$ and $f(x)$ are all continuous on $[a,b],$ we have the following boundary condition classifications. \n\n- Dirichlet:\n\n$$\ny(a)={\\gamma }_{1},\\,y(b)={\\gamma }_{2}\n$$\n\n- Neumann:\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(a)={\\gamma }_{1},\\,{y}^{′}(b)={\\gamma }_{2}\n$$\n\n- Robin (mixed):\n\n$$\n{\\alpha }_{1}y(a)+{\\beta }_{1}{y}^{′}(a)={\\gamma }_{1},\\,{\\alpha }_{2}y(b)+{\\beta }_{2}{y}^{′}(b)={\\gamma }_{2}\n$$\n\n- Periodic:\n\n$$\ny(a)=y(b),\\,{y}^{′}(a)={y}^{′}(b)\n$$\n\nwhere ${\\gamma }_{i},{\\alpha }_{i},$ and ${\\beta }_{i}$ are real numbers with $({\\alpha }_{i},{\\beta }_{i})\\ne (0,0).$ \n\nIn our case, we have the following boundary conditions, defined on $x=a=1$ and $x=b=3.$\n\n$$\ny(1)=0,\\,3y(3)+{y}^{′}(3)=6\n$$\n\nThese are Robin (mixed) boundary conditions." 13194139533488 17592186045585 true] [17592186402221 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402222 13194139533488 17592186045585 true] [17592186402221 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402223 13194139533488 17592186045585 true] [17592186402221 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402224 13194139533488 17592186045585 true] [17592186402221 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402225 13194139533488 17592186045585 true] [17592186402221 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402226 13194139533488 17592186045585 true] [17592186402221 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533488 17592186045585 true] [17592186402221 1077 "selection" 13194139533488 17592186045585 true] [17592186402221 1079 #edb/ref 17592186402223 13194139533488 17592186045585 true] [17592186402221 1080 #uuid "dd10be9b-3b17-5633-861a-6fa42ef0e0d8" 13194139533488 17592186045585 true] [17592186402222 1081 "Other" 13194139533488 17592186045585 true] [17592186402222 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533488 17592186045585 true] [17592186402222 1084 #uuid "51963deb-494b-5038-a567-d52bbae853d7" 13194139533488 17592186045585 true] [17592186402223 1081 "Robin" 13194139533488 17592186045585 true] [17592186402223 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533488 17592186045585 true] [17592186402223 1084 #uuid "ca70af21-75b9-54e1-a733-f7fe2f7fa12e" 13194139533488 17592186045585 true] [17592186402224 1081 "Neumann" 13194139533488 17592186045585 true] [17592186402224 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533488 17592186045585 true] [17592186402224 1084 #uuid "320aef74-4e39-5907-aac3-4ae1dafcfabd" 13194139533488 17592186045585 true] [17592186402225 1081 "Periodic" 13194139533488 17592186045585 true] [17592186402225 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533488 17592186045585 true] [17592186402225 1084 #uuid "99d38800-e0a0-56b4-b188-2bf47e62f659" 13194139533488 17592186045585 true] [17592186402226 1081 "Dirichlet" 13194139533488 17592186045585 true] [17592186402226 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533488 17592186045585 true] [17592186402226 1084 #uuid "b97382cb-a37a-52dd-8bc5-72cf2224232a" 13194139533488 17592186045585 true] [17592186402227 1068 #edb/ref 17592186402228 13194139533488 17592186045585 true] [17592186402227 1069 "q-339222" 13194139533488 17592186045585 true] [17592186402227 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533488 17592186045585 true] [17592186402227 1071 "The number of subscribers $N(t)$ to an e-learning platform varies according to the differential equation ${N}^{′}(t)=rN(t),$ where $t$ is the time since the platform was launched, measured in weeks, and $r>0.$ It is known that the number of subscribers doubles after the first four weeks. How long does it take for the number of subscribers to triple after the platform is launched? Round your answer to one decimal place." 13194139533488 17592186045585 true] [17592186402227 1072 #uuid "b562af2b-8343-5000-806c-d01887adea11" 13194139533488 17592186045585 true] [17592186402227 1074 "The general solution to the given differential equation is\n\n$$\nN(t)={N}_{0}{e}^{rt},\n$$\n\nwhere ${N}_{0}$ is the number of subscribers when $t=0.$\n\nLet ${t}_{1}$ be the time when the number of subscribers equals $3{N}_{0}.$ Then, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}N({t}_{1}) & =3{N}_{0}\\,⇒\\,{N}_{0}{e}^{r{t}_{1}}=3{N}_{0}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe solve this equation for ${t}_{1},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{N}_{0}{e}^{r{t}_{1}} & =3{N}_{0} \\\\ \\cancel{{N}_{0}}{e}^{r{t}_{1}} & =3\\cancel{{N}_{0}} \\\\ {e}^{r{t}_{1}} & =3 \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{r{t}_{1}}) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3) \\\\ r{t}_{1} & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡3 \\\\ {t}_{1} & =\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}{r}\\,\\,(∗)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now need to calculate $r.$ We're told that the number of subscribers doubles after the first four weeks the platform is launched. Therefore,\n\n$$\nN(4)=2{N}_{0}\\,⇒\\,{N}_{0}{e}^{4r}=2{N}_{0}.\n$$\n\nWe solve this equation for $r,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{N}_{0}{e}^{4r} & =2{N}_{0} \\\\ \\cancel{{N}_{0}}{e}^{4r} & =2\\cancel{{N}_{0}} \\\\ {e}^{4r} & =2 \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{4r}) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2) \\\\ r & =\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting this into $(∗)$ and evaluating, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{t}_{1} & =\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}{r} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}{(\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{4})} \\\\  & =\\frac{4\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2} \\\\  & ≈6.3,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to one decimal place." 13194139533488 17592186045585 true] [17592186402228 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402229 13194139533488 17592186045585 true] [17592186402228 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402230 13194139533488 17592186045585 true] [17592186402228 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402231 13194139533488 17592186045585 true] [17592186402228 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402232 13194139533488 17592186045585 true] [17592186402228 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402233 13194139533488 17592186045585 true] [17592186402228 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533488 17592186045585 true] [17592186402228 1077 "selection" 13194139533488 17592186045585 true] [17592186402228 1079 #edb/ref 17592186402229 13194139533488 17592186045585 true] [17592186402228 1080 #uuid "b4ae4df5-40ba-5454-aa69-0f62becda821" 13194139533488 17592186045585 true] [17592186402229 1081 "$6.3$ weeks" 13194139533488 17592186045585 true] [17592186402229 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533488 17592186045585 true] [17592186402229 1084 #uuid "386007b3-91ce-5982-8534-d31233322fdb" 13194139533488 17592186045585 true] [17592186402230 1081 "$6$ weeks" 13194139533488 17592186045585 true] [17592186402230 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533488 17592186045585 true] [17592186402230 1084 #uuid "0a01f341-43f3-528c-b811-0f8051a23c3c" 13194139533488 17592186045585 true] [17592186402231 1081 "$6.4$ weeks" 13194139533488 17592186045585 true] [17592186402231 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533488 17592186045585 true] [17592186402231 1084 #uuid "8ac92552-dc2b-5d29-986a-281a4e64330d" 13194139533488 17592186045585 true] [17592186402232 1081 "$6.5$ weeks" 13194139533488 17592186045585 true] [17592186402232 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533488 17592186045585 true] [17592186402232 1084 #uuid "c1738319-0cbe-5aa8-beb9-61d8c99fe62b" 13194139533488 17592186045585 true] [17592186402233 1081 "$6.2$ weeks" 13194139533488 17592186045585 true] [17592186402233 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533488 17592186045585 true] [17592186402233 1084 #uuid "aa2f0725-683a-50fc-855c-66c7d9ba756f" 13194139533488 17592186045585 true] [17592186402234 1068 #edb/ref 17592186402235 13194139533488 17592186045585 true] [17592186402234 1069 "q-339226" 13194139533488 17592186045585 true] [17592186402234 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139533488 17592186045585 true] [17592186402234 1071 "The value $V(t)$ of a tech device varies according to the differential equation ${V}^{′}(t)=-rV(t),$ where $t$ is the time, measured in years, and $r>0.$ It is known that the value reduces by one-half after the first year. How long does it take for the value to reduce to one-fifth of its original value? Round your answer to one decimal place." 13194139533488 17592186045585 true] [17592186402234 1072 #uuid "8375c335-8cf2-5c82-b2c9-770890e7d65a" 13194139533488 17592186045585 true] [17592186402234 1074 "The general solution to the given differential equation is\n\n$$\nV(t)={V}_{0}{e}^{-rt},\n$$\n\nwhere ${V}_{0}$ is the value when $t=0.$\n\nLet ${t}_{1}$ be the time when the value equals $\\frac{1}{5}{V}_{0}.$ Then, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V({t}_{1}) & =\\frac{1}{5}{V}_{0}\\,⇒\\,{V}_{0}{e}^{-r{t}_{1}}=\\frac{1}{5}{V}_{0}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe solve this equation for ${t}_{1},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{V}_{0}{e}^{-r{t}_{1}} & =\\frac{1}{5}{V}_{0} \\\\ \\cancel{{V}_{0}}{e}^{-r{t}_{1}} & =\\frac{1}{5}\\cancel{{V}_{0}} \\\\ {e}^{-r{t}_{1}} & =\\frac{1}{5} \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{-r{t}_{1}}) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{1}{5}) \\\\ -r{t}_{1} & =-\\operatorname{ln}⁡5 \\\\ {t}_{1} & =\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}{r}\\,\\,(∗)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now need to calculate $r.$ We're told that the value reduces by one-half after the first year. Therefore,\n\n$$\nV(1)=\\frac{1}{2}{V}_{0}\\,⇒\\,{V}_{0}{e}^{-r}=\\frac{1}{2}{V}_{0}.\n$$\n\nWe solve this equation for $r,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{V}_{0}{e}^{-r} & =\\frac{1}{2}{V}_{0} \\\\ \\cancel{{V}_{0}}{e}^{-r} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cancel{{V}_{0}} \\\\ {e}^{-r} & =\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{-r}) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\ -r & =-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2 \\\\ r & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting this into $(∗)$ and evaluating, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{t}_{1} & =\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}{r} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2} \\\\  & ≈2.3,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to one decimal place." 13194139533488 17592186045585 true] [17592186402235 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402236 13194139533488 17592186045585 true] [17592186402235 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402237 13194139533488 17592186045585 true] [17592186402235 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402238 13194139533488 17592186045585 true] [17592186402235 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402239 13194139533488 17592186045585 true] [17592186402235 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402240 13194139533488 17592186045585 true] [17592186402235 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533488 17592186045585 true] [17592186402235 1077 "selection" 13194139533488 17592186045585 true] [17592186402235 1079 #edb/ref 17592186402238 13194139533488 17592186045585 true] [17592186402235 1080 #uuid "fa46205e-ab90-5810-a697-993aab9f4c54" 13194139533488 17592186045585 true] [17592186402236 1081 "$2.4$ years" 13194139533488 17592186045585 true] [17592186402236 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533488 17592186045585 true] [17592186402236 1084 #uuid "10efe48b-a9f4-5aa8-8700-8513aef294db" 13194139533488 17592186045585 true] [17592186402237 1081 "$2$ years" 13194139533488 17592186045585 true] [17592186402237 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533488 17592186045585 true] [17592186402237 1084 #uuid "9483f82e-0758-5787-8ce2-48f26c64a23d" 13194139533488 17592186045585 true] [17592186402238 1081 "$2.3$ years" 13194139533488 17592186045585 true] [17592186402238 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533488 17592186045585 true] [17592186402238 1084 #uuid "85698021-f6eb-5674-af9e-26f88bf35ee6" 13194139533488 17592186045585 true] [17592186402239 1081 "$2.1$ years" 13194139533488 17592186045585 true] [17592186402239 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533488 17592186045585 true] [17592186402239 1084 #uuid "ec0b804f-53f8-5360-9835-166b54051187" 13194139533488 17592186045585 true] [17592186402240 1081 "$2.5$ years" 13194139533488 17592186045585 true] [17592186402240 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533488 17592186045585 true] [17592186402240 1084 #uuid "85d74bd3-72ef-5c17-a201-f97592fcc512" 13194139533488 17592186045585 true] [17592186402241 1068 #edb/ref 17592186402242 13194139533488 17592186045585 true] [17592186402241 1069 "q-339248" 13194139533488 17592186045585 true] [17592186402241 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533488 17592186045585 true] [17592186402241 1071 "The rate of increase ${E}^{′}(t)$ of the average monthly cost of electricity in a particular region varies according to the differential equation ${E}^{′}(t)=0.02E(t),$ where $t$ is the time, in years, since the year $2017.$ In $2021,$ the average monthly cost was $$124.50.$ What was the average monthly cost of electricity in $2017?$" 13194139533488 17592186045585 true] [17592186402241 1072 #uuid "d1d42a16-3984-5dae-bf8b-539545f414f5" 13194139533488 17592186045585 true] [17592186402241 1074 "The general solution to the given differential equation is\n\n$$\nE(t)={E}_{0}\\,{e}^{0.02t},\n$$\n\nwhere ${E}_{0}$ is the average monthly cost of electricity in $2017.$\n\nWe are given that the monthly residential electricity cost was $$124.50$ in $2021,$ so after $t=4$ years. Hence, substituting $t=4$ and $E(4)=124.50$ into our general solution and solving for ${E}_{0},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}E(4) & ={E}_{0}\\,{e}^{0.02\\cdot 4} \\\\ 124.50 & ={E}_{0}\\,{e}^{0.08} \\\\ {E}_{0} & =\\frac{124.50}{{e}^{0.08}} \\\\  & ≈114.93\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to the nearest cent.\n\nTherefore, the average monthly cost in $2017$ was $$114.93.$" 13194139533488 17592186045585 true] [17592186402242 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402243 13194139533488 17592186045585 true] [17592186402242 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402244 13194139533488 17592186045585 true] [17592186402242 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402245 13194139533488 17592186045585 true] [17592186402242 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402246 13194139533488 17592186045585 true] [17592186402242 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402247 13194139533488 17592186045585 true] [17592186402242 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533488 17592186045585 true] [17592186402242 1077 "selection" 13194139533488 17592186045585 true] [17592186402242 1079 #edb/ref 17592186402247 13194139533488 17592186045585 true] [17592186402242 1080 #uuid "b6cbfe2e-3815-5b36-b83f-63a2f8eb905b" 13194139533488 17592186045585 true] [17592186402243 1081 "$$31.13$" 13194139533488 17592186045585 true] [17592186402243 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533488 17592186045585 true] [17592186402243 1084 #uuid "98555ddd-6e37-50dd-95fe-cea932afb900" 13194139533488 17592186045585 true] [17592186402244 1081 "$$116.01$" 13194139533488 17592186045585 true] [17592186402244 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533488 17592186045585 true] [17592186402244 1084 #uuid "bcf3ab14-e63c-5a07-8f00-c6624545c11c" 13194139533488 17592186045585 true] [17592186402245 1081 "$$122.03$" 13194139533488 17592186045585 true] [17592186402245 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533488 17592186045585 true] [17592186402245 1084 #uuid "e23ede75-277e-5685-b92b-dcc0d6291e35" 13194139533488 17592186045585 true] [17592186402246 1081 "$$113.25$" 13194139533488 17592186045585 true] [17592186402246 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533488 17592186045585 true] [17592186402246 1084 #uuid "145dc5fb-065b-57b6-ab94-00b00d6949c4" 13194139533488 17592186045585 true] [17592186402247 1081 "$$114.93$" 13194139533488 17592186045585 true] [17592186402247 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533488 17592186045585 true] [17592186402247 1084 #uuid "41ca3324-7989-5875-90e2-784c63f6f17b" 13194139533488 17592186045585 true] [17592186402248 1068 #edb/ref 17592186402249 13194139533488 17592186045585 true] [17592186402248 1069 "q-339251" 13194139533488 17592186045585 true] [17592186402248 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533488 17592186045585 true] [17592186402248 1071 "Which of the following systems is an initial value problem?\n\nI. ${x}^{2}{y}^{″}-2{y}^{′}+y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x,\\,y(4)=1,\\,{y}^{′}(4)=-1$\nII. $x{y}^{″}+{y}^{′}-2y=9$\nIII. ${x}^{2}{y}^{″}-8x{y}^{′}+16y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x,\\,y(2)=0,\\,{y}^{′}(2)=3$" 13194139533488 17592186045585 true] [17592186402248 1072 #uuid "c104c7c7-be1b-5f7c-9495-548d3d354240" 13194139533488 17592186045585 true] [17592186402248 1074 "If a second-order differential equation for the function $y(x)$ is given with two conditions specified at the *same* location in the domain of $y,$ then this is an **initial value problem**.\n\nLet's go through each equation in turn.\n\n- The first system is an initial value problem. The differential equation is together with two conditions at the same location in the domain of $y(x)$ (i.e., at $x=4$).\n\n- The second system is not an initial value problem. It contains an equation only. No conditions are specified.\n\n- The third system is an initial value problem. The differential equation is together with two conditions at the same location in the domain of $y(x)$ (i.e., at $x=2$)." 13194139533488 17592186045585 true] [17592186402249 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402250 13194139533488 17592186045585 true] [17592186402249 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402251 13194139533488 17592186045585 true] [17592186402249 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402252 13194139533488 17592186045585 true] [17592186402249 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402253 13194139533488 17592186045585 true] [17592186402249 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402254 13194139533488 17592186045585 true] [17592186402249 1076 #e